  "reasoning": "The product features a carboxylic acid group at the 2-position of a substituted indole-2,3-dione (isatin) core. For deprotection reactions involving carboxylic acids, the standard retrosynthetic disconnection is to the corresponding ester protecting group, which is subsequently hydrolyzed. Methyl esters are the most common and straightforward protecting groups in this context. Replacing the -COOH moiety with a -COOCH3 group yields the methyl ester precursor. Acidic or basic hydrolysis of this ester would cleanly remove the protecting group and regenerate the target carboxylic acid, aligning perfectly with the deprotection reaction type.",
  "final_answer": "COC(=O)c1c[nH]c2c(F)cc(I)cc2c1=O"
}

